  "response_text": "Using a queue to store the TCBs in round-robing scheduling allows each thread to be processed in FIFO manner: The scheduler dequeues the next TCB to run, and if the thread is still supposed to run after its time slice, it is queued again. This approach is much simpler and more flexible than using an array. In addition, a circular queue may be used to make the process efficient by avoiding shifting and supporting continuous cycling through threads.\\n",
